IS  - 1942-597X (Electronic)
IS  - 1559-4076 (Linking)
VI  - 2020
DP  - 2020
TI  - AI Accelerated Human-in-the-loop Structuring of Radiology Reports.
PG  - 1305-1314
AB  - Rule-based Natural Language Processing (NLP) pipelines depend on robust domain 
      knowledge. Given the long tail of important terminology in radiology reports, it 
      is not uncommon for standard approaches to miss items critical for understanding 
      the image. AI techniques can accelerate the concept expansion and phrasal 
      grouping tasks to efficiently create a domain specific lexicon ontology for 
      structuring reports. Using Chest X-ray (CXR) reports as an example, we 
      demonstrate that with robust vocabulary, even a simple NLP pipeline can extract 
      83 directly mentioned abnormalities (Ave. recall=93.83%, precision=94.87%) and 47 
      abnormality/normality descriptions of key anatomies. The richer vocabulary 
      enables identification of additional label mentions in 10 out of 13 labels 
      (compared to baseline methods). Furthermore, it captures expert insight into 
      critical differences between observed and inferred descriptions, and image 
      quality issues in reports. Finally, we show how the CXR ontology can be used to 
      anatomically structure labeled output.
