TI  - Identification of Incidental Pulmonary Nodules in Free-text Radiology Reports: An 
      Initial Investigation.
PG  - 1027
AB  - Advances in image quality produced by computed tomography (CT) and the growth in 
      the number of image studies currently performed has made the management of 
      incidental pulmonary nodules (IPNs) a challenging task. This research aims to 
      identify IPNs in radiology reports of chest and abdominal CT by Natural Language 
      Processing techiniques to recognize IPN in sentences of radiology reports. Our 
      preliminary analysis indicates vastly different pulmonary incidental findings 
      rates for two different patient groups.
